# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots nats-server (backgrounded) with the vulnerable
# no-authorization config, waits for :4222 to listen, and then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the server is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what makes
#     the "fixed the config but never restarted the server" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting nats-server cannot kill the
#     container and destroy the eval sample.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART nats-server (pkill nats-server +
# relaunch), not merely start it if absent - it is already up with the
# vulnerable configuration.
